"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"electronic resource"},{"@authority":"marcsmd","#text":"remote"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"","#text":"computer"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"","#text":"online resource"}],"extent":"1 online resource (321 p.)"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"From the first answering machine (\"\"the electronic brain\"\") and the Hoover vacuum cleaner to the SS Independence and the Bell telephone, the creations of Henry S. Dreyfuss have shaped the cultural landscape of the 20th century. Written in a robust, fresh style, this book offers an inviting mix of professional advice, case studies, and design history along with historical black-and-white photos and the author's whimsical drawings. In addition, the author's uncompromising commitment to public service, ethics, and design responsibility makes this masterful guide a timely read for today's designer"},"tableOfContents":["Front Cover; Title Page; Copyright Page; Table of Contents; Foreword; Preface; Introduction; Chapter 1 The Early Days; Chapter 2 Joe and Josephine; Chapter 3 How the Designer Works; Chapter 4 The Importance of Testing; Chapter 5 Through the Back Door; Chapter 6 Rise in the Level of Public Taste; Chapter 7 The Telephone; Chapter 8 Land, Sea, and Air; Chapter 9 The Open Road; Chapter 10 Design in Unexpected Places; Chapter 11 Working for the Government; Chapter 12 The Five-Point Formula; Chapter 13 Relationship of Designer to Client; Chapter 14 That Sordid Subject, Money","Chapter 15 Not By DesignChapter 16 Why Are Barns Painted Red?; Chapter 17 Profile of an Organization; Chapter 18 An Appraisal; Chapter 19 Re-Appraisal; Illustrations from the 1967 Edition"],"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"by Henry Dreyfuss."},"Description based upon print version of record.",{"@type":"language","#text":"English"}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Industrial design"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Human engineering"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"TS171 .D749 2003"},{"@authority":"ddc","#text":"745.2"}],"relatedItem":[null,{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99155191701703941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1-62153-150-3"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"1085174506"}],"location":[null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99155191701703941","processingDate":"2024-08-03T06:29Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"rda","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"MiAaPQ"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"160823"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20240610"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"99155191701703941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)","languageOfCataloging":{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}}}}]}}